<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cotonou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cotonou is the largest city and economic capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>, on the coast between Lake Nokoué and the Atlantic. In the nineteenth century it was a small trading post of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Kingdom of Dahomey</a>, and disputes over treaties by which Dahomey had ceded it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-franco-dahomean-war">First Franco-Dahomean War</a> in 1890. Its port became the main outlet of the French colony, and it is the seat of Benin's government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cotonou.jpg" alt="Cotonou" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adoscam · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vue_panoramique_quartier_cadj%C3%A9houn-Cotonou_au_B%C3%A9nin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
